   <text:p text:style-name="P73"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P149" text:outline-level="1">Chapter 6</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T130">I don’t know what to make of you.” Alex says now that we are back in our suite for the evening.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T131">That’s probably the best you can make of me.” I say from across the dining table, “I’m sorry, but doubt and confusion are my bread and butter. Considering the situation you will be caught in the crossfire. You already were caught in the crossfire this morning.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T132">It’s alright.” Alex looks down at the surface of the table, “I’m sorry too. This situation has been stressful and I’ve been lashing out. Our entire lives have been upended but it feels like nobody cares. We’re not going home are we?”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T133">I sit back to consider that question, “I don’t know. Getting back to New York is possible but the journey would take upwards of a week and carries the real possibility getting lost forever. There’s also the question of whether there’s anything on Earth for us.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T134">Do you really think so? That the world has moved on without us?” tears began to gather in her eyes.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T135">Reaching over I put my hand on hers, “I doubt that everything is gone forever, but things can never go back to the way they were before all of this.” We talk a little more after retiring to Alex’s room. There are enough emotions for her to process already so I leave her to her sleep.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T136">What was that all about?” Noah worries when I return to the commons.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T136">Accepting the reality of the situation we’re in.” I reply.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T136">Is it really so bad?” Merin asks but with more genuine curiosity than offense.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T137">I take a moment to consider the girl before saying, “It’s not a comparison of worlds. We’ve all been ripped from our homes. We’ve lost everything with no guarantee of ever seeing Earth again. In the face of such loss grief is the natural response.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T137">Oh.” Merin says and captures the mood in the room. We all wander off to bed within the hour. Although I still have one conversation left for today.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T137">The System does not understand that this is my body and it shall obey me. The System using my mana, in my body under the orders of someone else without my permission is not acceptable. Some of the blame lies with me though. I have been reluctant to solidify my claim to avoid being trapped inside a human body. That fear seems so silly now.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T137">Resolve is nice but this still leaves the question of how. Grafting a separate body onto my very being is not something I have experience with. The only idea I have amounts to smashing them together and hoping it sticks. Of course magic is more conceptual than physical so there is no literal smashing. Shifting my true self to match my human body is the obvious first step.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:soft-page-break/><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T1">“</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4">Trait [Mana Leak] evolved into [Ruptured Manapool]”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P136">[Rupture Manapool]</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P136">The barrier keeping your mana under control is compromised. Raw Mana is freely flowing from your mana pool into your body and reeking havoc.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T137">The obvious second step is removing the barrier separating my two bodies. My claws tear through it but it tastes a little stale. Since the mana in my mana pool is mine and not simple raw mana it should not reek havoc. It does anyway but it should not. The System elements inside my body go crazy with the surge of mana before I pull it back into the mana pool through force of will. Jamming myself in the hole works as a temporary solution.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T137">Overlaying my human body in soul space like this is as close as I can get to it but there is still separation. The connection is much stronger but this body is just an imitation, not truly a part of me. There is no way around it if I want this body to become mine then I will also become its. If I want to influence the System then I have to open myself up to its influence. Just a crack at first but even those possibilities give me pause.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T1">“</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T5">You gained the trait [Kitsune Blood]!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P137">[Kitsune Blood]</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P137">The blood of a kitsune now flows through your veins. You are now more susceptible to its magics. The magical nature of the blood makes your body more resilient to the affects of other magic.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T138">This is the strangest use of shape shifting I have ever seen. Both hearts now beat together and blood flows freely between both bodies. Getting a fluid to flow between physical and soul space is easier than I thought. The System notices my efforts and now has a conduit into my true body. That is enough for now. It is time to sleep and let the changes unfold.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P142"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T139">The morning comes and I delight in the feeling of solidity and weight. I feel more real now. With synchronized bodies every movement has more momentum as well. That may even be literal. There is one thing ruining the morning. Remembering that Randel can read the name of traits.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T140">Alex looks better this morning and a short chat confirms it. Merin and Greg are nearby so it is time for something ill advised. I do not like my chances of keeping this trait hidden therefore revealing it on my terms is the better option.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T141">Hey Greg, are kitsune like reverse vampires?” I ask the man.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T141">The man gives me a dumbfounded look before asking, </text:span>“<text:span text:style-name="T141">What are you talking about?”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:soft-page-break/><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T141">I woke up with this [Kitsune Blood] trait so I was wondering it they bite people and inject blood or something.” </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T142">All eyes are on me for a while until Merin asks, “That doesn’t sound good. Shouldn’t you be more concerned?”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T142">I shrug, </text:span>“<text:span text:style-name="T142">I don’t know. It doesn’t hurt and the description just says that I’m more susceptible to kitsune magic. They’re basically pranksters, right? Being pranked harder isn’t that bad. Probably.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T143">I think we need to tell Randel.” Merin says and herds us out to morning practice.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T143">Me and Alex trail behind a little and she whispers, “I thought you were the kitsune?”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T143">I am.” I whisper back, “People always forget to mix uncertainty into their lies. Let someone else deal with the web.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T144">Merin tells Randel all about my new trait but he is less interested than I expected. Much as I disagree with the phrasing the way the System describes it as a negative puts him at ease. He does not even use [Inspect]. That suits me fine.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T144">Today’s exercise is uncomfortable. It would be painful without the flexibility of spirit I have as a shape shifter. The System is digging into me now that there is nothing separating me from this body. I could resist it but this is the plan. It is incorporating me into the statistics of this body and tying all three pieces closer together. The plan is working but the point of no return is fast approaching. Even now it would be hard to separate from the System.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P68"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T144">Your base Strength increased by 1!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P68"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T144">Your base Endurance increased by 3!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P68"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T144">Your base Dexterity increased by 2!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P68"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T144">Your base Constitution increased by 1!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T145">The second round of training after breakfast comes with a surprise. While the other team goes to their normal spots Randel calls mine over. Lined up beside him are 5 tied up foxes whimpering and struggling against their bonds. Maintaining a neutral expression is the best I can do because I know this is not heading anywhere pleasant.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T146">Randel wants us to kill them. It is a test to make sure we can fight with lethal intent. It makes sense as too many people freeze up in their first fight. It also feels personal that he choose foxes of all creatures though. I hope he meant to declare war.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T146">The process is brutal since none of my teammates know how to score a clean kill. Slitting the throat is a gruesome way to die but that is what people know. When it is my turn I do the same with a small twist. My hand touches the fox’s cheek and my mana floods his body. While the death is still messy I can at least hide the pain and calm his mind with an illusion.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:soft-page-break/><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T147">Once we return to our suite I plop down in the common area and Alex asks, “Are you OK? You seem a little out of it.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T148">The simple question takes me a moment to process, </text:span>“<text:span text:style-name="T148">No, I guess not. I don’t want to do this anymore.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T149">What? You think you can just quit? Run off to the forest or something?” Greg says, “News flash princess, you would have to kill animals there too. It was just a stupid fox get over yourself.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T149">I stand and walk up to Greg. Our eyes lock and my fist embeds itself in his stomach. Strength is not my forte but I can leverage two bodies at this point. Greg doubles over as I tell him, “I can kill just fine, Greg.” Noah grabs my arms and pulls me away from Greg. “Noah what are you doing?”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T149">You need to calm down, Kim.” Noah says, “Violence isn’t the answer. We can get through this, but not if we fight each other.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T149">If you say so.” I sigh.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T150">Was that really necessary?” Alex questions and leads me to the dining table.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T150">No, but it felt good.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T151">Alex checks the surrounds then whispers, “Is it because they were foxes?”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T151">Yeah, but it’s not just that. I’ve been ordered to kill other ones before. I’ve even had to hunt and kill things I didn’t want to. Having to do it for someone I don’t respect though. That’s the problem. I’ve run out of patience for Randel.” I admit. From there Alex turns the conversation to flowers as a nice distraction. Botany is something of a hobby for her.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T152">Noah comes over with a stern look and demands, “You need to apologize. Greg is really upset.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T152">No.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T153">But why?”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T153">If he is going to side with our abductors, then I will treat him as such.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7"/>
