   <text:p text:style-name="P74"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P150" text:outline-level="1">Chapter 7</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T153">Tonight I test whether I can burn the System. I already know physical illusions can work on the people here regardless of power. My claws and fangs can touch it but fire is my preferred weapon. The remains of my mana pool makes a perfect target since it needs to go anyway.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T1">“</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">Your base Willpower increased by 5!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T1">“</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">You gained the trait [Foxfire]!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P138">[Foxfire]</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P138">You<text:span text:style-name="T162">r</text:span> mana can manifest as a mystical flame. This flame dances on the border between illusion and reality. You can control how hot it is for each thing it touches. Willpower increases the maximum temperature.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T13">The plan goes awry immediately and my head is pounding from the System’s intrusion. I do not even know how it latched onto my willpower but it is painful and permanent. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T14">Flopping back on my bed I let the implication bounce around in my head and increase my headache.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><text:span text:style-name="T14"><text:tab/></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T15">The second attempt also fails but in a less painful way. This time a likely intentional defense of the System gets in the way. When I summon my fox fire the ambient mana prevents it from leaving the physical realm. Traits from the System are not allowed to target spiritual elements. There may be exceptions but it is clear that I misunderstood the Systems idea of raw mana. It may be malleable but the ambient mana in this world is ultimately the System’s. That is annoying but it is better than having unstable mana floating around everywhere.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9"><text:tab/>There is a simple solution in this instance. If I can not burn my own mana pool from the outside then I will do it from the inside. <text:span text:style-name="T154">This time it works and my fox fire burns through the mana barrier surrounding my hands. While the process does not take long I can feel the System trying to repair the breech leaving me sitting on my bed with flaming hands. Loose ends of the magical construct writhe as their work is continually destroyed until one of them sticks onto me. Unlike before with the attributes the damaged end leaves an opening for me to exploit. I smile as soon all of the loose ends are captured giving me access to the inner working of my System.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T1">“</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T7">You gained the trait…”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P10"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T155">I can feel the System trying to figure out what happened but that gets put on hold when the door to my room opens. Greg stands there staring at me in surprise. Before it turns even more awkward I try to speak but a ripple of magic runs through my body. It is less invasive than Randel’s [Inspect] but still not something I appreciate. When I go to resist it everything goes wrong.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T156">The familiar pain of the System merging with me is present. This time it comes with an overload of every sense. No thought can make it through the shear chaos until it finally ends. By that time I am exhausted and sore both mentally and physically. At some point I fell on the floor too and made enough noise to bring everyone here.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P11"><text:soft-page-break/><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T1">“...</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T9">[Claws]!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P11"><text:span text:style-name="T1"><text:tab/>“</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">Your base Intelligence has increased by 8!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:span text:style-name="T8"><text:tab/></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T157">“I didn’t do anything to her!” Greg protests.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T157">You’re trying to tell me she just has a seizure as you just happen to wander past her door in the middle of the night?” Alex glares at the man, “Bullshit!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T158">Maybe we should just calm down and figure out hat happened first.” Noah suggests only for Alex to round on him next. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P13"><text:tab/>Merin pushes her way past now once she notices me awake. “Are you OK?” she asks before placing a hand on my shoulder and running magic through me, “What happened?” It really is much nicer than Greg’s attempt. Healing pretty much just gives my own body the energy to fix itself.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T159">Tired. Sore.” I reply, “Greg showed up. Used something like [Inspect]. Tried to resist. Mixed results.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T160">Merin gasps and turns to Greg demanding, “You used [Inspect] on her?”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T161">No! It’s just [Appraisal]!” Greg stammers.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T161">So you did do something!” Alex jumps in, “I knew it!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T162">Now hold on, we don’t even know why yet.” Noah says, “Maybe he has a good reason.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T162">Yeah, her hands were on fire so I had to check her status.” Greg says.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T162">But that’s illegal!” Merin cries, “You aren’t allowed to see the status of other humans without permission! It’s a violation of privacy!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T162">She’s not even human!” he shouts, “Look, her claws are showing! I told you she was the kitsune!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P12"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T162">All eyes, mine included, turn to my hands where there are in fact claws replacing my finger nails. That explains the strange System message from before. I forgot to check the information on these [Claws], too.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P139">[Claws]</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P139"><text:span text:style-name="T163">Sharp claws extend from the ends of your fingers</text:span>. Intelligence increases their sharpness.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T162">Neat” I say and roll onto my back to better admire my claws. The connection between sharpness and intelligence is a mystery for later.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T162">OK, that is a little suspicious.” Noah says.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T162">Are you really a beast kin?” Merin gasps.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T162">A what?” I ask, “No, I’m pretty sure I’m just tired.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:soft-page-break/><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T163">Merin blinks at me before telling Greg, “Regardless, it’s still an incredibly rude thing to do.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T163">Oh no. How dare I be rude to someone that punched me in the face.” Greg mocks. This is the point where I check out of the conversation. Pulling my blanket onto the floor with me I curl up to sleep. The seizure wiped out so much energy that it is no problem even with a heated argument raging in the same room.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P143"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T163">Waking up brings a mixture of emotions. I’m stiff from sleeping on the ground and annoyed with Greg. On the other hand I can feel the flows of magic on my hands and regained my claws. I spend a few minutes just extending and retracting them before realizing that should be impossible. Foxes have retractable claws but humans do not. It is not worth figuring out how to make them work with human fingers when one can just shape shift them away.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T163">Things click together at that point. It is shape shifting and that is why intelligence increases the sharpness. Testing that sharpness on the wooden door is delightful. My claws gouge out furrows in the wood with no problems.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T164">I am the first awake but when Alex gets up she comes over and says, “I can’t believe that creep. What did he even think he was doing sneaking into your room?”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T164">Nothing good.” I say, “He’s wearing through my patience. If he keeps pushing for a fight, I’m going to end him.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T164">It takes a moment for Alex to process my words, “Whoa, hold on. That’s a pretty extreme. You aren’t serious are you?”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T164">I am. Honestly, I didn’t expect him to try confronting me in the middle of the night. Maybe things will work out nicely, but there is a serious possibility one of us ends up dead.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T165">The next event of the day happens at morning training. After Merin talks with Randel the man calls me over holding a pair of bracelets. They look a lot like shackles but have no chain and a dark red gem. “Congratulations, you are the first beastkin outsider.” Randel says, “It’s a good thing I ordered some suppressors for you since you’re already starting fights.” Holding up the bracelets up he continues, “These will suppress the beast spirit and keep its taint under control. Do not remove them. Do not get in anymore fights. Understand?”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T166">I glare at him but agree anyway. This is not a fight I want. Especially after feeling the amount of mana rushing through my fingers toward him. It is an obscene amount of magical power for a base line and terrifies me with its implications.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P14"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T167">The bracelets go on but have no effect until I help them out. With no exposed piece of the System below my forearms there is no purchase for the enchantment. That is good news for later but it </text:span><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T167">is too risky to sabotage them right in front of Randel. Only when the effect sets in does the gem start glowing.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P15"><text:tab/>The effect is not as advertised. Instead my anger at Randel evaporates. Not a shred of indignation or contempt exists in me at the orders he gives. When he gives a little praise at the end of the morning workout it feels good. The horror at the thought of what these would do to someone unaware is not affected by the bracelets. These people have an entire race of slaves and expect me to be part of it.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P63"/>
