     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table4.A3" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P123">Traits</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table4.D1" table:number-columns-spanned="3" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P117"><text:span text:style-name="T162">[Claws] [Foxfire] </text:span>[Hekate’s Blessing] <text:span text:style-name="T169">[HP Barrier (Hidden)] [Kitsune Blood] [Ruptured Manapool] [Weapon Handling] </text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:covered-table-cell/>
     <table:covered-table-cell/>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="P77"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P153" text:outline-level="1">Chapter 10</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P71">“<text:span text:style-name="T208">You gained the trait [Shapeshifter]!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P71">“<text:span text:style-name="T208">Your Endurance increased to 18!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P71">“<text:span text:style-name="T208">Your Intelligence increased to 22!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P71">“<text:span text:style-name="T208">The trait [Claws] merged with [Shapeshifter]!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P71">“<text:span text:style-name="T208">You gained the trait [Kitsunetsuki]!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P71">“<text:span text:style-name="T208">The traits [HP Barrier (Hidden)], [Kitsune Blood], and [Ruptured Manapool] merged with [Kitsunetsuki]!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P71">“<text:span text:style-name="T208">Your Willpower increased to 21!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P71">“<text:span text:style-name="T208">You gained the trait [Illusionist]!”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P72"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T28">The past month allowed me to sort out my System. The most important part was returning to a vulpine form. Hands were great but being stuck in the form rubbed the wrong way. The shapeshifting went deeper than flesh though and allowed me to make the System a part of myself. Kitsunetsuki was an odd choice of term but technically accurate </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T29">I guess</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T28">. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T29">A kitsune does possess this system.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T28"> Either way it gave me the ability to choose whether my magics are affected by the mana currents in Prahoria. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T29">Illusions are a real option again.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P26"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T209">Alex’s time was much more mixed. She did inherit [Foxfire] and beautiful vulpine eyes that can see the magic of the world from the soul bond we have. Hekate’s training was closer to camping but it will be useful regardless. The real problem is that she got more withdrawn as time progressed.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P26"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T210">Are you ready to head out?” I ask in travel form. While my true form is a seven tailed fox the size of a draft horse, that is not convenient. A single tailed normal sized fox is much less noticeable even if I keep my white fur.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P26"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T210">I guess.” Alex says, “It’s not like I’m getting much out of this place anyway.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P26"><text:tab/><text:span text:style-name="T210">I frown but Hekate appears with her hand on Alex’s shoulder and says, “There’s not much I can do for you in your state.”</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P26"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T211">Oh, I’m sorry. I was just abandoned by my family after being murdered and kidnapped, but I guess I’ll try harder.” Alex huffs.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P26"><text:tab/>“<text:span text:style-name="T212">Oh child, there’s no problem with grieving what’s lost. However, the world will not stand still for you.” Hekate says and pulls an athame from her stola, “You will need to decide whether you wish to pick up the piece and continue living or not.” What can best be described as a ripple of disillusionment passes through the space. It has little effect on me as I am well aware of Hekate’s nature. On the other hand Alex blanches and tears form in her eyes as she is faced with the full weight of the goddess’ offer. </text:span><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T212">More important the ripple makes it clear that there is no malice or manipulation in Hekate’s actions. Terrible as the options are the choice is up to Alex and Alex alone.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P26"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P26"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P26"><text:s/></text:p>
